(6316492, 930474, 43463, '<td valign="top">Fabulous landscape that is very beautiful to observe. I can feel the wind and the chill. A good shot but there are two things holding this back from being a <i>great</i> shot. First off is that there seems to be a lack of sharpness to the scene (oddly the coulds appear in good focus). I''m thinking that mayhap the sharpness is there on the original large size and this is a case where resizing a large file in one stop has some loss of detail. It is better to do the resizing of a large image file in two or three stops with a sharpen in between - you suffer less loss of detail that way. If the less tack sharp is not due to resizing you can recover a bit of the lost detail with use of USM (unsharp mask /sharpen feature) but be careful not to go overboard. Lastly, the composition could be even stronger if you played up the strength of using the bridge as a leading line in the photo. I think it would be a stronger composition if you captured the full arch of the bridge where the other arch point/base springs out of the bottom left hand corner - the lines would then lead the eye to the span of beauty beyond.</td>', 'Fabulous landscape that is very beautiful to observe. I can feel the wind and the chill. A good shot but there are two things holding this back from being a great shot. First off is that there seems to be a lack of sharpness to the scene (oddly the coulds appear in good focus). I''m thinking that mayhap the sharpness is there on the original large size and this is a case where resizing a large file in one stop has some loss of detail. It is better to do the resizing of a large image file in two or three stops with a sharpen in between - you suffer less loss of detail that way. If the less tack sharp is not due to resizing you can recover a bit of the lost detail with use of USM (unsharp mask /sharpen feature) but be careful not to go overboard. Lastly, the composition could be even stronger if you played up the strength of using the bridge as a leading line in the photo. I think it would be a stronger composition if you captured the full arch of the bridge where the other arch point/base springs out of the bottom left hand corner - the lines would then lead the eye to the span of beauty beyond.', '2011-02-16 08:11:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6316516, 930069, 113411, '<td valign="top">Really a fabulous capture!</td>', 'Really a fabulous capture!', '2011-02-16 08:30:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6316542, 931062, 43463, '<td valign="top">She has gorgeous big eyes &amp; an elegant long neck in this lovely portrait. The B&amp;W really plays up those features - I instantly thought of the classic photo shot of Twiggy when I saw this. Simple, elegant and well done portrait of this young lady.</td>', 'She has gorgeous big eyes & an elegant long neck in this lovely portrait. The B&W really plays up those features - I instantly thought of the classic photo shot of Twiggy when I saw this. Simple, elegant and well done portrait of this young lady.', '2011-02-16 08:51:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6316548, 934213, 43463, '<td valign="top">I love the colors and the composition of this shot. The greens, yellows and browns of the tree and bird really pops off the plan white backdrop - makes me think of the first blush of spring. Love how you composed/captured the shot with the bird centered in the natural triangle shaped frame that is the branches of this tree. Also great capture that you caught this bird with a seed/food in it''s beak - nice bit of added visual interest. My only critique is that the frame of the image is so big that it engulfs the image - I think the image is strong enough to stand out on it''s own with little to no border.</td>', 'I love the colors and the composition of this shot. The greens, yellows and browns of the tree and bird really pops off the plan white backdrop - makes me think of the first blush of spring. Love how you composed/captured the shot with the bird centered in the natural triangle shaped frame that is the branches of this tree. Also great capture that you caught this bird with a seed/food in it''s beak - nice bit of added visual interest. My only critique is that the frame of the image is so big that it engulfs the image - I think the image is strong enough to stand out on it''s own with little to no border.', '2011-02-16 08:56:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6316551, 934774, 114233, '<td valign="top">If this doesnt do as well as you were hoping for - these are things that get to me: The sign on the right is chopped off, The door doesnt have a bottom/base, the rope top left is a little distracting, it doesnt look that sharp. Looks too much like a quick snapshot to be DPC friendly.<br/>The leading line of the roof is nice and the placement of the lamp is good too.</td>', 'If this doesnt do as well as you were hoping for - these are things that get to me: The sign on the right is chopped off, The door doesnt have a bottom/base, the rope top left is a little distracting, it doesnt look that sharp. Looks too much like a quick snapshot to be DPC friendly.The leading line of the roof is nice and the placement of the lamp is good too.', '2011-02-16 08:58:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(6316554, 930220, 107730, '<td valign="top">This is easily one of my favourite photos... Great shot!</td>', 'This is easily one of my favourite photos... Great shot!', '2011-02-16 09:00:19.000000', NULL, 1),
