(6318067, 930905, 65438, '<td valign="top">Nice reflections and I like the koi in the shot.</td>', 'Nice reflections and I like the koi in the shot.', '2011-02-17 00:53:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318068, 933851, 65438, '<td valign="top">Very moody.  Love this.</td>', 'Very moody.  Love this.', '2011-02-17 00:53:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318070, 931175, 30364, '<td valign="top">Excellent.  Deceptively offhand, because it''s actually perfectly executed.  I reckon you''ve thought this out much more carefully than an undiscriminating first glance would suggest.  Best mug shot of the year and it goes onto my 2010 imaginary wall.  Thank you.</td>', 'Excellent.  Deceptively offhand, because it''s actually perfectly executed.  I reckon you''ve thought this out much more carefully than an undiscriminating first glance would suggest.  Best mug shot of the year and it goes onto my 2010 imaginary wall.  Thank you.', '2011-02-17 00:56:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318077, 930220, 30364, '<td valign="top">I don''t like city skyline at night pictures, but this one is a splendid exception.  Just enough of everything, not too much of anything.  And the bold tilt outweighs the by now tiresome frame as well.  On my imaginary 2010 wall for sure.  Thank you.</td>', 'I don''t like city skyline at night pictures, but this one is a splendid exception.  Just enough of everything, not too much of anything.  And the bold tilt outweighs the by now tiresome frame as well.  On my imaginary 2010 wall for sure.  Thank you.', '2011-02-17 01:01:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318084, 930103, 30364, '<td valign="top">I admit to being captivated by this picture, as I am by others of similar ambition.  It''s the same feeling I get from looking at contemporary sculpture, or from eating really good sushi ... that my experience of the thing is a part of the thing, that it is meaningless without my engagement with it.  Or that I am meaningless without my engagement with it, which is even more exciting.  Here the faint marks seem to be more about memory than about any current reality; and the title is so apt for that mood.  I''d put this on my imaginary 2010 wall, and be stirred every time I passed by it.  Thank you.</td>', 'I admit to being captivated by this picture, as I am by others of similar ambition.  It''s the same feeling I get from looking at contemporary sculpture, or from eating really good sushi ... that my experience of the thing is a part of the thing, that it is meaningless without my engagement with it.  Or that I am meaningless without my engagement with it, which is even more exciting.  Here the faint marks seem to be more about memory than about any current reality; and the title is so apt for that mood.  I''d put this on my imaginary 2010 wall, and be stirred every time I passed by it.  Thank you.', '2011-02-17 01:12:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318085, 932915, 30364, '<td valign="top">While I''m not a fan of the slightly idealised processing, the inspired composition stamps all over my petty bias and leaves it bleeding.  Finally a guitar photograph at DPC that is worth a longer look.  And this one is worth several, which is why I''m hanging in on my imaginary 2010 wall.  Thank you.</td>', 'While I''m not a fan of the slightly idealised processing, the inspired composition stamps all over my petty bias and leaves it bleeding.  Finally a guitar photograph at DPC that is worth a longer look.  And this one is worth several, which is why I''m hanging in on my imaginary 2010 wall.  Thank you.', '2011-02-17 01:17:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318088, 935489, 30364, '<td valign="top">Best landscape, without a doubt.  Onto my imaginary 2010 wall for further admiration.  Thank you.</td>', 'Best landscape, without a doubt.  Onto my imaginary 2010 wall for further admiration.  Thank you.', '2011-02-17 01:18:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318100, 930049, 30364, '<td valign="top">To take a creature in captivity and yet dignify it by its circumstances is a remarkable achievement.  So many such pictures manage to be merely mawkish.  This one is sad, also gracious and ultimately beautiful, but certainly never sentimental.  Congratulations.  It''s on my 2010 imaginary wall. Thank you.</td>', 'To take a creature in captivity and yet dignify it by its circumstances is a remarkable achievement.  So many such pictures manage to be merely mawkish.  This one is sad, also gracious and ultimately beautiful, but certainly never sentimental.  Congratulations.  It''s on my 2010 imaginary wall. Thank you.', '2011-02-17 01:30:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318101, 935482, 30364, '<td valign="top">Just a flat-out good photograph of a beautiful, lively lady.  A sense of great admiration between photographer and subject, flowing in both directions.  It goes onto my imaginary 2010 wall.  Thank you.</td>', 'Just a flat-out good photograph of a beautiful, lively lady.  A sense of great admiration between photographer and subject, flowing in both directions.  It goes onto my imaginary 2010 wall.  Thank you.', '2011-02-17 01:33:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318107, 930048, 30364, '<td valign="top">Wonderful!  I loved looking at it, which is why I must immediately hang it on my imaginary 2010 wall.  Thank you.</td>', 'Wonderful!  I loved looking at it, which is why I must immediately hang it on my imaginary 2010 wall.  Thank you.', '2011-02-17 01:34:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318153, 931358, 86218, '<td valign="top">Nice simple comp and love the B&amp;W processing.</td>', 'Nice simple comp and love the B&W processing.', '2011-02-17 02:17:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318154, 931053, 30364, '<td valign="top">This is one of those delightful photographs that looks initially like an offhand shot of nothing much, and yet turns out to become more and more and more as the many layers of meaning and interest unfurl themselves.  Some of the great street photographs are like that (I mean universally, not DPC''s current street challenge) ... they look mild and yet reveal themselves to be profound, or at least special.  Here the characters are arrayed as if for some kind of performance, a ''street'' version of a chorus line perhaps, and I am irresistibly drawn to imagine speech bubbles all over the place, like in a comic strip.  All those overlapping conversations, thoughts and asides.  All the roles people adopt.  Making your picture, for me, a wonderful tilt at communication and modern manners.  <i>The Importance of Being Earnest</i> for the 21st century.  This now hangs on my imaginary 2010 wall, entertaining me and confounding the janitors.  Thank you.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=800078" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg"/></a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2014-10-01 05:00:38.</i></td>', 'This is one of those delightful photographs that looks initially like an offhand shot of nothing much, and yet turns out to become more and more and more as the many layers of meaning and interest unfurl themselves.  Some of the great street photographs are like that (I mean universally, not DPC''s current street challenge) ... they look mild and yet reveal themselves to be profound, or at least special.  Here the characters are arrayed as if for some kind of performance, a ''street'' version of a chorus line perhaps, and I am irresistibly drawn to imagine speech bubbles all over the place, like in a comic strip.  All those overlapping conversations, thoughts and asides.  All the roles people adopt.  Making your picture, for me, a wonderful tilt at communication and modern manners.  The Importance of Being Earnest for the 21st century.  This now hangs on my imaginary 2010 wall, entertaining me and confounding the janitors.  Thank you.', '2011-02-17 02:19:06.000000', '2014-10-01 06:00:38.000000', 1),
(6318168, 935389, 30364, '<td valign="top">So wonderfully bizarre and beautifully executed too.  It will probably be largely dismissed as a novelty entry, which will be a huge underestimation of it.  But that''s really the very point it''s making, yes?  The comfort of sameness and familiarity versus the discomfort of perceptual audacity?  I love your photograph, and am thrilled to now see it hanging on my imaginary 2010 wall.  It''s looking pretty bloody singular even there, as well.  Thank you.</td>', 'So wonderfully bizarre and beautifully executed too.  It will probably be largely dismissed as a novelty entry, which will be a huge underestimation of it.  But that''s really the very point it''s making, yes?  The comfort of sameness and familiarity versus the discomfort of perceptual audacity?  I love your photograph, and am thrilled to now see it hanging on my imaginary 2010 wall.  It''s looking pretty bloody singular even there, as well.  Thank you.', '2011-02-17 02:25:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318252, 934198, 114682, '<td valign="top">Really very nice view and execution, it just look''s somehow overprocessed to me.</td>', 'Really very nice view and execution, it just look''s somehow overprocessed to me.', '2011-02-17 06:53:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318255, 930052, 113419, '<td valign="top">this is beautiful, makes me wanna go there</td>', 'this is beautiful, makes me wanna go there', '2011-02-17 07:12:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318256, 933247, 113419, '<td valign="top">excellent</td>', 'excellent', '2011-02-17 07:15:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318284, 932028, 43463, '<td valign="top">This is a great cultural portrait - along the lines of what one would see when turning the pages of National Geographic Magazine. Great clouds that seems to frame and radiate out from her. Now as much as I say that this is National Geographic worthy I still have a critique that would improve the composition and thus a stronger response in your audience (oh, man can she be critical right:-) ). I know that the full body shot captures the wonderful colors in the skirt but it is at the expense of showing the story written on her face and a lesser degree minimalizing her livelihood to tiny subject barely visible in the backdrop. Bring us up close and personal with this shepherdess - a crop that is just under the ''T'' of her belt would still show some of the colorful skirt but it would now bring the story written in her eyes and face that much closer...and the sheep would be a bit more noticible.</td>', 'This is a great cultural portrait - along the lines of what one would see when turning the pages of National Geographic Magazine. Great clouds that seems to frame and radiate out from her. Now as much as I say that this is National Geographic worthy I still have a critique that would improve the composition and thus a stronger response in your audience (oh, man can she be critical right:-) ). I know that the full body shot captures the wonderful colors in the skirt but it is at the expense of showing the story written on her face and a lesser degree minimalizing her livelihood to tiny subject barely visible in the backdrop. Bring us up close and personal with this shepherdess - a crop that is just under the ''T'' of her belt would still show some of the colorful skirt but it would now bring the story written in her eyes and face that much closer...and the sheep would be a bit more noticible.', '2011-02-17 08:02:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318296, 931953, 126446, '<td valign="top">It''s HDR or just really saturated, and the filter or filter effect is really obvious.  I think it''s a beautiful scene, but the filter use / HDR / editing makes it look like a cartoon to me.</td>', 'It''s HDR or just really saturated, and the filter or filter effect is really obvious.  I think it''s a beautiful scene, but the filter use / HDR / editing makes it look like a cartoon to me.', '2011-02-17 08:26:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318298, 931917, 87808, '<td valign="top">gorgeous processing, would love to see how 9</td>', 'gorgeous processing, would love to see how 9', '2011-02-17 08:26:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318300, 933355, 87808, '<td valign="top">Fabulous processing, so rich and warm, well done 9</td>', 'Fabulous processing, so rich and warm, well done 9', '2011-02-17 08:27:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318302, 934935, 126446, '<td valign="top">Beautiful!  I love it.  My photo for this contest is also from Japan, but this is just incredible.  Do you live here as well?  9</td>', 'Beautiful!  I love it.  My photo for this contest is also from Japan, but this is just incredible.  Do you live here as well?  9', '2011-02-17 08:28:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318303, 933661, 87808, '<td valign="top">Adore it, looks like the Cape, love the  stark harsh lines of the fence versus the softness of the dunes. 9</td>', 'Adore it, looks like the Cape, love the  stark harsh lines of the fence versus the softness of the dunes. 9', '2011-02-17 08:28:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318304, 935467, 87808, '<td valign="top">Impressive</td>', 'Impressive', '2011-02-17 08:28:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318305, 931206, 126446, '<td valign="top">This is great!  Way to capture a real moment.  I just wish I would have thought of making a sign like that! (the one on the right, not the middle!)  haha</td>', 'This is great!  Way to capture a real moment.  I just wish I would have thought of making a sign like that! (the one on the right, not the middle!)  haha', '2011-02-17 08:29:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318306, 935389, 87808, '<td valign="top">Still think this is very daring and makes you look more than twice, love your mind!</td>', 'Still think this is very daring and makes you look more than twice, love your mind!', '2011-02-17 08:29:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318307, 932978, 87808, '<td valign="top">LOL</td>', 'LOL', '2011-02-17 08:32:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318308, 931358, 87808, '<td valign="top">10 ribbon winner right here</td>', '10 ribbon winner right here', '2011-02-17 08:32:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318309, 935676, 126446, '<td valign="top">Is this real?  It really looks like a plastic model.  I think it''s because the stars are clearly moving for minutes, but two things which normally move quite a bit in outdoor wind (the windmill and flowers) are perfectly still and sharp.  That tension makes it look completely unreal to me, but it is still a very nice composition and combination of color.  This was a hard one to vote on!</td>', 'Is this real?  It really looks like a plastic model.  I think it''s because the stars are clearly moving for minutes, but two things which normally move quite a bit in outdoor wind (the windmill and flowers) are perfectly still and sharp.  That tension makes it look completely unreal to me, but it is still a very nice composition and combination of color.  This was a hard one to vote on!', '2011-02-17 08:33:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318311, 935402, 43463, '<td valign="top">What a great find of capturing a landscape photo of a painter painting a landscape. Love the composition. It shows the painter near enough to the tree that I can assume she had chosen the spot for shade but has been there for a long time that the shade has moved; the passage of time is demonstrative in the photograph. Now I do have a critique: the sephia tones I feel just don''t complement the composition. The yellow/gold tones are more dull than warm. I think B&amp;W might have been a better choice for then the play of light and shadow upon the tree and folliage/bushes would have been more visually present. And I also think that the mountain range would not blend into the sky and get lost in the composition.</td>', 'What a great find of capturing a landscape photo of a painter painting a landscape. Love the composition. It shows the painter near enough to the tree that I can assume she had chosen the spot for shade but has been there for a long time that the shade has moved; the passage of time is demonstrative in the photograph. Now I do have a critique: the sephia tones I feel just don''t complement the composition. The yellow/gold tones are more dull than warm. I think B&W might have been a better choice for then the play of light and shadow upon the tree and folliage/bushes would have been more visually present. And I also think that the mountain range would not blend into the sky and get lost in the composition.', '2011-02-17 08:38:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318326, 931358, 93421, '<td valign="top">Best of luck! (Not voting)</td>', 'Best of luck! (Not voting)', '2011-02-17 09:00:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318331, 930863, 110108, '<td valign="top">i doubt it might get Dq''ed but if it does not then it''s an excellent comosition and execution ...10</td>', 'i doubt it might get Dq''ed but if it does not then it''s an excellent comosition and execution ...10', '2011-02-17 09:03:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318333, 931101, 30364, '<td valign="top">A really wonderful portrait that tells me you''ve taken the trouble to study the work of great photographers of the past, and to understand what they did any why.   This is a gloriously anti-digital photograph, not just because of the distinctly analogue appearance of both the subject and of the ''print'', but also because in concept it recalls an era when photographers had to make their impact with simple tools and clear ideas (instead of an oversupply of tools and an absence of ideas, as is the current fashion).  In some ways this disarmingly direct portrait is in the style of Diane Arbus, in spite of the fact that this young bloke is rather more conventional-looking than were most of her subjects.  Definitely a place for this one on my imaginary wall of 2010 excellence.  Thank you.</td>', 'A really wonderful portrait that tells me you''ve taken the trouble to study the work of great photographers of the past, and to understand what they did any why.   This is a gloriously anti-digital photograph, not just because of the distinctly analogue appearance of both the subject and of the ''print'', but also because in concept it recalls an era when photographers had to make their impact with simple tools and clear ideas (instead of an oversupply of tools and an absence of ideas, as is the current fashion).  In some ways this disarmingly direct portrait is in the style of Diane Arbus, in spite of the fact that this young bloke is rather more conventional-looking than were most of her subjects.  Definitely a place for this one on my imaginary wall of 2010 excellence.  Thank you.', '2011-02-17 09:05:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318342, 934145, 93421, '<td valign="top">Love the image but feel that it would benefit from a 90 degree rotate to the right</td>', 'Love the image but feel that it would benefit from a 90 degree rotate to the right', '2011-02-17 09:11:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318357, 932167, 30364, '<td valign="top">I really like this photograph.  There''s a similar picture by someone good (it might be Eugène Atget) of a cathedral (it might be Notre Dame) seem through the branches of a tree (don''t know what kind of tree), and yours is equally pleasing for the same reason; surprisingly satisfying juxtaposition, that elevates it from the humdrum.  This goes onto my imaginary wall of 2010 excellence.  Thank you.</td>', 'I really like this photograph.  There''s a similar picture by someone good (it might be Eugène Atget) of a cathedral (it might be Notre Dame) seem through the branches of a tree (don''t know what kind of tree), and yours is equally pleasing for the same reason; surprisingly satisfying juxtaposition, that elevates it from the humdrum.  This goes onto my imaginary wall of 2010 excellence.  Thank you.', '2011-02-17 09:38:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318366, 935681, 98339, '<td valign="top">such a lovely country scene...</td>', 'such a lovely country scene...', '2011-02-17 09:46:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318368, 935679, 30364, '<td valign="top">Well, yes indeed it is ... in style, in spirit, and also (with a bit of imagination) in cartographic terms.  It''s a beautiful thing, and effortlessly transcends the photographic medium.  But I''d hang it on my imaginary wall of 2010 photographic excellence, because I don''t have a wall of transcendent excellence yet.  This definitely goes up there when I do.  Thank you.</td>', 'Well, yes indeed it is ... in style, in spirit, and also (with a bit of imagination) in cartographic terms.  It''s a beautiful thing, and effortlessly transcends the photographic medium.  But I''d hang it on my imaginary wall of 2010 photographic excellence, because I don''t have a wall of transcendent excellence yet.  This definitely goes up there when I do.  Thank you.', '2011-02-17 09:46:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318369, 934748, 30364, '<td valign="top">Magnificent moggy.  The intensity of the gaze makes me feel as if I were a ball of wool, or a mouse.  The only cat portrait on my imaginary 2010 wall.  Thank you.</td>', 'Magnificent moggy.  The intensity of the gaze makes me feel as if I were a ball of wool, or a mouse.  The only cat portrait on my imaginary 2010 wall.  Thank you.', '2011-02-17 09:47:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6318372, 935644, 30364, '<td valign="top">Beautiful.  A glimpse inside creation (I mean real creation of course, not that other nonsense). There''s something very moving about it, something about the fragility of existence.  The tenuous hold we have on our own future.  But its tone is optimistic, not defeatist.  I''d be elevated every time I saw it, which I will because it is definitely on my imaginary 2010 wall of excellence.  Thank you.</td>', 'Beautiful.  A glimpse inside creation (I mean real creation of course, not that other nonsense). There''s something very moving about it, something about the fragility of existence.  The tenuous hold we have on our own future.  But its tone is optimistic, not defeatist.  I''d be elevated every time I saw it, which I will because it is definitely on my imaginary 2010 wall of excellence.  Thank you.', '2011-02-17 09:49:52.000000', NULL, 1),
