(6320976, 931036, 30214, '<td valign="top">delightful image!</td>', 'delightful image!', '2011-02-19 16:04:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6320985, 930222, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Toning aside, there is something nostalgic about this image. I also like how unfettered it is while remaining crafted and purposeful. Strangely the image isn''t without menace - like a representation of a visitation.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Not much at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: I really like this - despite its composition it feels uncommonly well balanced.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Toning aside, there is something nostalgic about this image. I also like how unfettered it is while remaining crafted and purposeful. Strangely the image isn''t without menace - like a representation of a visitation. Critical stuff: Not much at all. Overall: I really like this - despite its composition it feels uncommonly well balanced.', '2011-02-19 16:26:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(6320988, 935389, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Alicia, I liked this image when I saw it before and I am still a fan. The back story to the image has stayed with me and I find your image resonates with its meaning and motive. The selective focus, the darkly burnt borders and the mauve-ish hues all work so well.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Its slight off-centredness troubles me just a tad.<br/> <br/>Overall: Thoughtful, careful, well-crafted work.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Alicia, I liked this image when I saw it before and I am still a fan. The back story to the image has stayed with me and I find your image resonates with its meaning and motive. The selective focus, the darkly burnt borders and the mauve-ish hues all work so well. Critical stuff: Its slight off-centredness troubles me just a tad. Overall: Thoughtful, careful, well-crafted work.', '2011-02-19 16:30:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(6320994, 930863, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: This is very well done, I love how the making of the letters has lit the scene and all of the questions you have placed in front us (each without answers). I like how, grass aside, there is hardly any colour in the image yet it is clear it isn''t monochrome.. The writing itself adds a great deal of menace - its hanging-in-space weirdness (despite it being clear how it was done), the meaning of the word and what it means to whoever is inside and whoever is outside - almost like we are being invited to view the scene through the eyes of a potential killer...<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing<br/> <br/>Overall: Fascinating and powerful.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: This is very well done, I love how the making of the letters has lit the scene and all of the questions you have placed in front us (each without answers). I like how, grass aside, there is hardly any colour in the image yet it is clear it isn''t monochrome.. The writing itself adds a great deal of menace - its hanging-in-space weirdness (despite it being clear how it was done), the meaning of the word and what it means to whoever is inside and whoever is outside - almost like we are being invited to view the scene through the eyes of a potential killer... Critical stuff: Nothing Overall: Fascinating and powerful.', '2011-02-19 16:37:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(6320996, 934674, 19944, '<td valign="top">the cat blinked</td>', 'the cat blinked', '2011-02-19 16:40:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(6320998, 932090, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: A hugely engaging photo - such potential for story building here and the technicals are superb. Great coloration, subtle tone mapping, light, exposure, focus etc... all spot on. The touching of the glass transforms the image, through that potential for self-harm, the subject seems vulnerable. Also, his age is difficult to place precisely, perhaps its because we don''t get to see his whole face.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing<br/> <br/>Overall: Really excellent work.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: A hugely engaging photo - such potential for story building here and the technicals are superb. Great coloration, subtle tone mapping, light, exposure, focus etc... all spot on. The touching of the glass transforms the image, through that potential for self-harm, the subject seems vulnerable. Also, his age is difficult to place precisely, perhaps its because we don''t get to see his whole face. Critical stuff: Nothing Overall: Really excellent work.', '2011-02-19 16:41:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(6321000, 934728, 50695, '<td valign="top">I''m too close to this photo to vote on it, but it does look outstanding.</td>', 'I''m too close to this photo to vote on it, but it does look outstanding.', '2011-02-19 16:42:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6321002, 933409, 30861, '<td valign="top">In many ways a wildly pleasing image, but it has been mangled technically; your use of dodge and burn is glaringly obvious, unfortunately.</td>', 'In many ways a wildly pleasing image, but it has been mangled technically; your use of dodge and burn is glaringly obvious, unfortunately.', '2011-02-19 16:42:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(6321005, 930620, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I know I''ve seen this image before and I liked it then too. Once again I''m bound to comment on the girl behind (the star of the image) and how she is looking on in disbelief - and then we notice her shoes and we wonder who she is kidding with her knuckle duster heels!<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I think it would be more powerful with a bit more contrast.<br/> <br/>Overall: Excellent street shot.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I know I''ve seen this image before and I liked it then too. Once again I''m bound to comment on the girl behind (the star of the image) and how she is looking on in disbelief - and then we notice her shoes and we wonder who she is kidding with her knuckle duster heels! Critical stuff: I think it would be more powerful with a bit more contrast. Overall: Excellent street shot.', '2011-02-19 16:44:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(6321006, 932818, 19944, '<td valign="top">the processing looks kind of funky</td>', 'the processing looks kind of funky', '2011-02-19 16:45:17.000000', NULL, 1),
