(6324061, 931036, 30861, '<td valign="top">This is really nice, Ben. It has a real old-school, Pt. Lobos type feel to it, like a 1950''s Minor White, or perhaps a Wynn Bullock. Well done!</td>', 'This is really nice, Ben. It has a real old-school, Pt. Lobos type feel to it, like a 1950''s Minor White, or perhaps a Wynn Bullock. Well done!', '2011-02-21 03:51:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(6324062, 934706, 30861, '<td valign="top">Helluva shot, Alan. I''m amazed you didn''t level the horizon, though :-( I can''t see any  reason not to.</td>', 'Helluva shot, Alan. I''m amazed you didn''t level the horizon, though :-( I can''t see any  reason not to.', '2011-02-21 03:52:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(6324063, 930222, 30214, '<td valign="top">this photo reminded me this masterpiece<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=741229" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/15000-19999/16241/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_741229.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/15000-19999/16241/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_741229.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/15000-19999/16241/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_741229.jpg"/></a> <br/>the boy has grown... and lost his smile. For me, it is actually the opposite of the horizon.. the wall. He is being slowly squeezed out of the frame.</td>', 'this photo reminded me this masterpiece the boy has grown... and lost his smile. For me, it is actually the opposite of the horizon.. the wall. He is being slowly squeezed out of the frame.', '2011-02-21 03:57:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(6324064, 935359, 126446, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone!  This is one of my first challenges on DPReview. <br/> <br/>Just a couple comments about the photo:<br/> <br/>This was taken in JPEG and was very minimally edited.  I bumped the contrast, slightly shifted the blue, vignetted a bit, and sharpened, and that''s about it.  It was not cropped, not HDRd, no other tricks.  <br/> <br/>I took a couple shots in landscape (horizontal), but there is a park on one side and a city on the other, that I felt distracted too much from the main point of the image.  I took several shots and this was the best one. <br/> <br/>Thanks again for all the comments!<br/> <br/>//www.flickr.com/photos/efranzjapan/<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-02-21 03:58:10.</i></td>', 'Thanks everyone!  This is one of my first challenges on DPReview.  Just a couple comments about the photo: This was taken in JPEG and was very minimally edited.  I bumped the contrast, slightly shifted the blue, vignetted a bit, and sharpened, and that''s about it.  It was not cropped, not HDRd, no other tricks.   I took a couple shots in landscape (horizontal), but there is a park on one side and a city on the other, that I felt distracted too much from the main point of the image.  I took several shots and this was the best one.  Thanks again for all the comments! //www.flickr.com/photos/efranzjapan/', '2011-02-21 03:57:41.000000', '2011-02-21 03:58:10.000000', 0),
(6324068, 933661, 108069, '<td valign="top">Incredible image. Moody, lugubrious, foreboding, chilled desolation. Wonderful tones.</td>', 'Incredible image. Moody, lugubrious, foreboding, chilled desolation. Wonderful tones.', '2011-02-21 04:07:45.000000', NULL, 0),
