(6324349, 934841, 44877, '<td valign="top">Seriously? Sub-5? Wow. So far I''d rate this the most underappreciated image in the challenge. I still love it a lot.</td>', 'Seriously? Sub-5? Wow. So far I''d rate this the most underappreciated image in the challenge. I still love it a lot.', '2011-02-21 09:33:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(6324351, 934706, 3102, '<td valign="top">It''s interesting you would mention that, actually!<br/> <br/>I had struggled with that aspect of this shot for quite a while before submitting it.  In the first version I submitted, I did indeed straighten the horizon properly.  But the way the wave curves, it actually made it feel unbalanced and tilted, oddly enough.  The more I looked at it with a perfectly straight horizon, the more it bothered me that it <i>appeared</i> to be off.<br/> <br/>I rotated it just a couple degrees, and it felt more balanced to me.  Just another weird attribute of this shot, I guess.  I was curious to see if anyone else would comment on that, and was surprised no one had said anything about it during voting.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Bear_Music:</b></div><hr/><i> Helluva shot, Alan. I''m amazed you didn''t level the horizon, though :-( I can''t see any  reason not to. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'It''s interesting you would mention that, actually! I had struggled with that aspect of this shot for quite a while before submitting it.  In the first version I submitted, I did indeed straighten the horizon properly.  But the way the wave curves, it actually made it feel unbalanced and tilted, oddly enough.  The more I looked at it with a perfectly straight horizon, the more it bothered me that it appeared to be off. I rotated it just a couple degrees, and it felt more balanced to me.  Just another weird attribute of this shot, I guess.  I was curious to see if anyone else would comment on that, and was surprised no one had said anything about it during voting. Originally posted by Bear_Music: Helluva shot, Alan. I''m amazed you didn''t level the horizon, though :-( I can''t see any  reason not to. ', '2011-02-21 09:35:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(6324352, 935701, 44877, '<td valign="top">That had to be yours - amazing!</td>', 'That had to be yours - amazing!', '2011-02-21 09:36:15.000000', NULL, 0),
